  ***********************************************************

  
  ADF will solve the Kohn-Sham equations with constraint      
  electron density (KSCED) for the nonfrozen subsystem (rho1) 
  
  The effect of the frozen environment is described by an 
  effective embedding potential in these equations. 
  The method and the implementation are described in the 
  references given above.
  
  W A R N I N G 
  ============= 
  
  In the current implementation, only the electron density of the embedded 
  system is calculated. Therefore, only properties that depend directly    
  on the density (e.g., dipole moments) are available.                     
  In addition, the TDDFT extension allows the calculation of electronic    
  excitation energies and polarizabilities, and the calculation of         
  NMR shieldings is possible using the NMR program.                        
  The calculation of NMR spin-spin coupling constants is possible using the
  CPL program, however, the embedding contributions to the kernel for the
  determination of the perturbed orbitals is neglected at the moment.
  The calculation of FDE energies relies on the calculation of total
  energies for the embedded system and all caveats for total energy
  evaluations apply. In pure embedding calculations, the interaction energy
  with the environment requires a full supermolecular integration grid. The
  calculation of a full subsystem DFT energy is implemented only for the
  case of two active fragments.
  
  EVERYTHING ELSE IS NOT YET IMPLEMENTED 
  THE RESULTS OBTAINED FOR OTHER PROPERTIES MIGHT BE MEANINGLESS
  
  In particular, energy gradients are not yet available 
  
  ----------------------------------------------
   General options for Frozen Density Embedding 
  ----------------------------------------------
  
  Using frozen-density embedding integration grid (default)
  (as described in J. Phys. Chem. A 109 (2005), 7805)
  
  -------------------------------------------------
   Extension of Frozen Density Embedding to TDDFT  
  -------------------------------------------------
  
  TDDFT extension will be used
  
  Literature:
   - M.E. Casidas, T.A. Wesolowsi, Int. J. Quantum Chem. 96 (2004), 577. 
   - T.A. Wesolowski, J. Am. Chem. Soc. 126 (2004), 11444. 
  
  ---------------------------------------
   Nonadditive kinetic energy functional 
  ---------------------------------------
  
  For an assessment of functionals for weakly interacting systems see:
    T.A. Wesolowski, J. Chem. Phys. 106 (1997), 8516.   
  Based on this study, the use of PW91K is recommended 
  
  Nonadditive kinetic energy functional used in the embedding potential: 
  
  PW91k:
    GGA functional based on PW91 exchange functional           
    kinetic energy reparametrization by Lembarki and Chermette 
    [Phys. Rev. A 50 (1994), 5328]                             
  
  
  ---------------------------------------------
   Nonadditive exchange-correlation functional 
  ---------------------------------------------
  
  exchange-correlation part of the embedding potential approximated using: 
 LDA
  
